# Repository text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# This is hygiene, not the mechanism. Proofbound artifact identity does not depend on it:
# scripts/_artifact_identity.py normalizes CRLF to LF before hashing, so a CRLF checkout
# produces the same recorded identity with or without this file. The rule exists so the
# committed bytes and the canonical form agree, which keeps `sha256sum` on a checkout a
# usable cross-check against the ledger.
#
# Deliberately NOT `-text`: that would disable Git's text handling for these files —
# degrading diff, merge and eol behavior for first-class human-readable documents — purely
# to stabilize a hash that is already stable by construction.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
